                        "form_id": "9e59ef67-e8b0-4708-b026-406c3da759dd",
                        "entry_id": "bb6e1c1b-79a7-3cd0-a900-f8f711f01fc5",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "short-form"
                        ],
                        "form": "уби́йственны"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bd4db964-b72a-3be6-910d-0eaa0ba44a94",
                        "entry_id": "bb6e1c1b-79a7-3cd0-a900-f8f711f01fc5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "то же, что смертоносный; убивающий, причиняющий смерть"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3d6822c6-e0ff-41d6-8fe7-ef842a2d0245",
                                "sense_id": "bd4db964-b72a-3be6-910d-0eaa0ba44a94",
                                "text": "Первый из них давал указания на устройство мины в Малой Садовой и относительно количества необходимого для нее динамита; он изобрел и сделал убийственный метательный снаряд; без Кибальчича, несмотря на второстепенную роль его с юридической точки зрения, быть может не было бы преступления."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a062a05a-1485-49c1-aac0-8988f770345b",
                                "sense_id": "bd4db964-b72a-3be6-910d-0eaa0ba44a94",
                                "text": "И бросился с полком под убийственный огонь мгновенно затрещавших со всех сторон ружей и пулеметов."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "aa89c2bd-fa9c-3a95-8576-bce4e1f13a26",
                        "entry_id": "bb6e1c1b-79a7-3cd0-a900-f8f711f01fc5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен. крайне тяжёлый, неприятный; вредный, губительный; невыносимо плохой"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "860879e8-dcf5-45fc-b1a2-5df61fe7ffea",
                                "sense_id": "aa89c2bd-fa9c-3a95-8576-bce4e1f13a26",
                                "text": "Убийственная новость"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "916dcb83-0495-4eaf-9b81-0af8f0aa9bd9",
                                "sense_id": "aa89c2bd-fa9c-3a95-8576-bce4e1f13a26",
                                "text": "И, конечно, он давно оставил бы Москву и стал бы жить в Петербурге, если бы не убийственный для его легких климат нашей северной столицы."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4c076ab0-0de1-406a-b5bb-de069b76a887",
                                "sense_id": "aa89c2bd-fa9c-3a95-8576-bce4e1f13a26",
                                "text": "Брошен в климат, убийственный для здоровья, в общество, удушающее душу, я не нахожу в товарищах людей, которые бы могли понять мои мысли, не нахожу в азиатцах, кто бы разделил мои чувства."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e01e7736-8021-31c0-b173-cdeb0ab7bc49",
                        "entry_id": "bb6e1c1b-79a7-3cd0-a900-f8f711f01fc5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен., разг. чрезмерный, из ряда вон выходящий, необыкновенный по силе проявления, воздействия"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "da25445b-01b9-491e-8af6-12a6da06ec80",
                                "sense_id": "e01e7736-8021-31c0-b173-cdeb0ab7bc49",
                                "text": "На полюсах он, конечно, ниже, но туда убийственный жар заносят жидкие и газовые течения, т. е. тамошние океаны и атмосферы."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5661a08f-094c-3ba6-8a22-b30394480c19",
                        "entry_id": "bb6e1c1b-79a7-3cd0-a900-f8f711f01fc5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен., разг. резкий, беспощадный, уничтожающий"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0dd068d4-1dd9-48cc-9291-d8580798a295",
                                "sense_id": "5661a08f-094c-3ba6-8a22-b30394480c19",
                                "text": "―Ах да, ― отвечала Софи, кидая на меня убийственный взгляд."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8f9d7f8c-2f53-4463-8553-2508c77322ee",
                                "sense_id": "5661a08f-094c-3ba6-8a22-b30394480c19",
                                "text": "И тут европейский индивидуализм, столь убийственный для настоящей индивидуальности, т. е. для исключительного, обособленного, сильного и выразительного развития характеров!"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "dea8fc68-36dd-44a7-878d-3ba592291d11",
                        "source_entry_id": "bb6e1c1b-79a7-3cd0-a900-f8f711f01fc5",
                        "target_lang_word": "murderous",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "murderous",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cb7c5a02-919c-3eaa-aaad-06031f494488",
                                        "entry_id": "af7b685a-b8cf-3c8a-9069-277b908882c5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of, characterized by, or pertaining to murder or murderers."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e10ac084-e259-4853-b6e7-6774bc99e313",
                                                "sense_id": "cb7c5a02-919c-3eaa-aaad-06031f494488",
                                                "text": "Aſſaſſinat: m. A murther, or murtherous act committed for gaine, or in hope of a revvard; alſo, a ſuddaine aſſault, made of ſet purpoſe, and vvith a murtherous intent, although th' aſſaulted be not killed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "20b8edb5-6ebd-4cfa-92e8-5d3f966671c8",
                                                "sense_id": "cb7c5a02-919c-3eaa-aaad-06031f494488",
                                                "text": "Every time I heard the bell strike, that denotes the time on board a ship, I full of terror counted the hours until four o'clock; feeling sure that when that hour came, my enemies would begin their murderous attack."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "66d70621-3c4f-488a-bb77-c4f8ae181842",
                                                "sense_id": "cb7c5a02-919c-3eaa-aaad-06031f494488",
                                                "text": "While Harley had been in no way responsible for Pelton's murderous attack upon Yesler, public opinion held him to account."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7cd77eac-9884-4f38-a573-02170558115a",
                                                "sense_id": "cb7c5a02-919c-3eaa-aaad-06031f494488",
                                                "text": "[O]ne minute this \"Jihadi John\" was struggling to get by, and get accepted, in drizzly England, unemployed with a mortgage to pay and a chip on his shoulder, and the next he stands in brilliant Levantine sunlight, where everything is clear and etched, at the vanguard of some Sunni Risorgimento intent on subjecting the world to its murderous brand of Wahhabi Islam."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "325d9c41-85c3-3f50-a5ff-be8d2b030ca4",
                                        "entry_id": "af7b685a-b8cf-3c8a-9069-277b908882c5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a person: intending or likely to commit murder; bloodthirsty, homicidal."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a2970060-a13d-496b-bc93-0ae6a8b1e4ca",
                                                "sense_id": "325d9c41-85c3-3f50-a5ff-be8d2b030ca4",
                                                "text": "murderous behaviour"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6b389571-c7ea-4d70-835d-32e8fe260242",
                                                "sense_id": "325d9c41-85c3-3f50-a5ff-be8d2b030ca4",
                                                "text": "She gave me a murderous look."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "71d3585c-7e29-481d-b75f-92f1fcc33b24",
                                                "sense_id": "325d9c41-85c3-3f50-a5ff-be8d2b030ca4",
                                                "text": "Is any man loth to leave his priſon? or to remove his dwelling from cruel enemies? or to ſcape the hands of murderous robbers? Do we take the world indeed for our priſon? our cruel, ſpoyling, murderous foe? and yet we are loth to leave it?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1195c1c2-c7bd-4585-84ca-f167561ff8e7",
                                                "sense_id": "325d9c41-85c3-3f50-a5ff-be8d2b030ca4",
                                                "text": "De Salez her Husband ſtriving and ſtrugling for life againſt the pangs of death; fear and haſt (contrary to her intent and mind) had ſo made his murtherous wifes hand ſhake and tremble, as ſhe did not ſo fully cut his throat-bole, but he could yet both cry and groan, which he did very mournfully, and which indeed was ſoon over-heard by a man and a maid-ſervant of his, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "502533ad-0ebb-4ab2-802c-c69c5eba3201",
                                                "sense_id": "325d9c41-85c3-3f50-a5ff-be8d2b030ca4",
                                                "text": "Adam alſo was the High Prieſt, and received Authority from God, to teach the ſucceeding Generations of Men how to worſhip God, and what Sacrifices were to be offered by Cain and Abel, and all Poſterity. By which Sacrifices were brought into all Nations, to apply the Blood of the Lamb, ſlain from the foundation of the World, in the unalterable Purpoſes of God, to the Conſciences of all Men for the Remiſſion of their Sins, and to Excommunicate murderous Cain from the preſence of the Lord, […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3e37f61c-78b0-364f-948f-9760399cc452",
                                        "entry_id": "af7b685a-b8cf-3c8a-9069-277b908882c5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of an object: used to commit murder; capable of causing death; deadly, fatal."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "often"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d3bf0a7-45ab-4be2-84d9-69c36b69b458",
                                                "sense_id": "3e37f61c-78b0-364f-948f-9760399cc452",
                                                "text": "The rapid ſquadrons ſwift as thought engage, / And ſeek the hoſtile troops who ſhun their rage, / 'Midſt the thick clouds which ſmoak and duſt afford / With dreadful luſtre gleams the murderous ſword; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "04d0bf58-f01d-486a-a1e0-d08c76907e39",
                                                "sense_id": "3e37f61c-78b0-364f-948f-9760399cc452",
                                                "text": "In neceſſary ſelf-defence men have a right to kill their aſſailants. But duelling is unlawful and murderous, a remain of the ancient Gothic barbarity."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9965c591-a3b8-4c5d-b77a-77bf77c7d655",
                                                "sense_id": "3e37f61c-78b0-364f-948f-9760399cc452",
                                                "text": "In street fighting at close quarters a gun of this kind is very murderous and ought to do a terrible amount of destruction."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2c1e1469-52d5-3f80-b253-f5e8449234ed",
                                        "entry_id": "af7b685a-b8cf-3c8a-9069-277b908882c5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Very difficult."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6a908f08-26a7-46a1-847e-76eeba4aa52e",
                                                "sense_id": "2c1e1469-52d5-3f80-b253-f5e8449234ed",
                                                "text": "a murderous exam"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6595a25a-affb-4599-9d01-50d1154ae2f4",
                                                "sense_id": "2c1e1469-52d5-3f80-b253-f5e8449234ed",
                                                "text": "conditions were murderous"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
